* sg13g2-ldo -- SG13CMOS5L E1 DC operating-point extraction bench (issue #158).
* Generated from
* sim/ldo-cmos5l-pvt-sweep/testbench/tb_e1op_cmos5l.spice.tmpl by
* sim/ldo-cmos5l-pvt-sweep/run_e1op.sh -- do not edit a generated
* netlist-snapshots/*.spice file directly. Full methodology, quantity list,
* sign conventions and the pole-estimate limitations are in
* sim/ldo-cmos5l-pvt-sweep/README.md "E1 DC operating points (issue #158)"
* and spec/decision-records/DR-0015-...md's follow-up brief (experiment E1);
* this header is a short pointer.
*
* Generated for: corner=mos_ss temp=125C res=res_bcs
* cap=cap_typ Cc_w=170u (nominal)
* PDK: ihp-sg13cmos5l /tmp/kt155/src/pdks/ihp-open-pdk (see sim/pdk-cmos5l.json for the pinned release)
* OSDI models: /tmp/kt155/src/pdks/ihp-open-pdk/ihp-sg13cmos5l/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi (built by sim/tools/build-osdi.sh)
* Design netlist under test (frozen at this repo's git sha in the record):
*   /home/ubuntu/GitHub/sg13g2-ldo/.loom/worktrees/issue-158/design/sg13cmos5l/netlist/ldo_core_cmos5l.spice
*
* WHAT THIS BENCH IS: experiment E1 of DR-0015's follow-up brief -- a DC
* operating-point extraction of the SG13CMOS5L LDO at the four selected
* points P1/P2/P5/P6 (pass-device I_d/g_ds/V_eaout, divider current, and
* the error-amplifier devices' operating-point quantities needed to
* estimate the two low-frequency pole mechanisms). It measures the
* diagnosis's declared unknowns; it changes no schematic, no layout, no
* spec row and no verdict. DR-0015 stays Proposed.
*
* CIRCUIT: byte-for-byte the flattened tb_loopgain_cmos5l bench (issue #21;
* loop broken at FB with a 0 V AC source -- FBAMP is a MOSFET gate, so the
* break draws zero current and the DC operating point is the closed loop's;
* run_sweep.sh's assert_loopgain_topology_sync() diffs the four mirrored
* instantiation lines and the break against the generated netlist every
* run), PLUS two additions that cannot perturb that operating point:
*
* 1. The non-invasive divider replica from tb_dcsweep_cmos5l (issue #31):
*    an ideal unity VCVS copy of VOUT driving byte-identical rhigh legs
*    through a 0 V ammeter Vdivsense. ngspice cannot report a branch
*    current inside an rhigh/r3_cmc subcircuit, so i(vdivsense) is how the
*    divider's standing current -- and, with v(vout), its per-leg
*    resistance -- is measured. The replica's node set (REPTOP/REPT/REPFB)
*    is disjoint from the circuit under test and draws zero current from
*    VOUT (a VCVS input), so Iq, the operating point and every other
*    quantity are unchanged.
* 2. A `.save` card naming the device operating-point parameters this
*    experiment exports. With the OSDI PSP103 devices, saveable parameter
*    names are (verified against ngspice-46 + the pinned PDK's psp103.osdi):
*    `[ids]` (drain current; saved into the rawfile as `i(@n.<path>[ids])`),
*    `[gm]`, `[gds]`, `[cgs]`, `[cgd]`, `[cdd]` and `[vth]` (saved as
*    `v(@n.<path>[vth])`). The bare `[id]` and `[vbs]` spellings create
*    ZERO-LENGTH vectors and a single zero-length saved vector makes
*    ngspice's rawfile `write` fail outright ("no writable vector found"),
*    so they must never be added to the save list.
*
* Device-instance naming (the wrdata token contract): every MOS in this
* bench instantiates the PDK subckt wrapper `sg13_hv_pmos`/`sg13_hv_nmos`,
* whose inner PSP device is `nsg13_hv_pmos`/`nsg13_hv_nmos` (read from
* models/sg13g2_moshv_mod.lib at the pinned commit). Hierarchical paths:
* `@n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids]` (top level), `@n.xamp.xminp.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm]`
* (inside the Xamp subckt). The .save card and the wrdata line below name
* exactly these paths; batch_backend.py's e1op branch resolves the rawfile
* vectors (exact name, then the i()/v()-wrapped spelling) and fails closed
* on any token it cannot find.
*
* ANALYSIS: `dc vin 3.299 3.301 0.001` -- a three-point DC sweep bracketing
* the operating point (Vin = 3.30 V). It is one operating-point extraction
* with a +/-1 mV quasi-static neighbourhood around it, not a line-regulation
* measurement: the CSV's middle row (v-sweep exactly 3.3) IS the operating
* point the E1 record reduces. The sweep exists because (a) a one-point
* axis gives ngspice's `.meas dc ... AT=` "out of interval" (the liveness
* measurement would fail), and (b) the two extra rows give the reducer a
* free finiteness/continuity check. analysis.kind stays "dc" so the same
* liveness-measurement machinery as every other bench applies; there is no
* `.meas op` in ngspice.
*
* SIGN/UNIT CONVENTIONS (the record states them per quantity):
* - `[ids]` is this PDK's PSP103 OSDI magnitude-signed drain current:
*   POSITIVE when the device conducts, for BOTH polarities (verified
*   against ngspice-46 + psp103.osdi in the --validate probe: the pass
*   device delivering 1 mA reports ids = +1.0048e-3 A). An off device
*   reports tiny positive leakage. Never expect a negative ids; the
*   reducer treats one as a unit/sign mistake. gm, gds, cgs, cgd > 0;
*   cdd may be NEGATIVE (PSP charge-based cap sign); PMOS [vth] < 0.
* - i(vdivsense) > 0 = current into the replica divider (REPTOP -> REPT).
* - i(vin) < 0 while the rail delivers current (ngspice source-branch
*   sign); |i(vin)| = total supply current (pass + erramp + Men/Mbdis).
* - i(vbreak) ~ 0 (the FB/FBAMP break draws no current -- the record
*   reports it as the break-validity check).
* - All voltages in V, currents in A, gm/gds in S, caps in F, from the
*   deck's own units. Temperatures in C (klt's axis), tnom = 27 C.
*
* ENABLE (issue #67/#89, same as tb_loopgain): EN tied to VIN (enabled,
* regulating state); the G1 pull-down inside Xamp is off (ENB at VDD).

.lib "/tmp/kt155/src/pdks/ihp-open-pdk/ihp-sg13cmos5l/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib" mos_ss
.lib "/tmp/kt155/src/pdks/ihp-open-pdk/ihp-sg13cmos5l/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib" res_bcs
.lib "/tmp/kt155/src/pdks/ihp-open-pdk/ihp-sg13cmos5l/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerCAP.lib" cap_typ

.options temp=125 tnom=27

.include "/home/ubuntu/GitHub/sg13g2-ldo/.loom/worktrees/issue-158/design/sg13cmos5l/netlist/ldo_core_cmos5l.spice"

Vin VIN 0 dc 3.30
Vref VREF 0 dc 0.90 ac 0
Ibias IBIAS 0 dc 2u
* Operating point (issue #64 convention, substituted by run_e1op.sh; the
* four E1 points are DR-0015's P1/P2/P5/P6: ESR = 0 everywhere).
Iload VOUT 0 dc 0
Cout VOUT 0 1u
* ESR=0: Cout wired directly to ground (all four E1 points)

* --- flattened ldo_core_cmos5l, loop broken at FB. Byte-for-byte the
* tb_loopgain_cmos5l template's copy (FB -> FBAMP on Xamp's first pin and
* the inserted Vbreak excepted, exactly as there) -- run_sweep.sh's
* assert_loopgain_topology_sync() diffs this block against the generated
* netlist on every run. ---
Vgnd VSS 0 dc 0
XMpass VOUT EAOUT VIN VIN sg13_hv_pmos w=2800u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1
XRtop VOUT FB VSS rhigh w=1e-6 l=25.43e-6 m=1 b=7
XRbot FB VSS VSS rhigh w=1e-6 l=25.43e-6 m=1 b=7
Vbreak FB FBAMP 0 ac 1
Xamp FBAMP VREF EAOUT VIN VSS IBIAS EN ldo_erramp_cmos5l
XMen EAOUT EN VIN VIN sg13_hv_pmos w=40u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1
XMbdis IBIAS EN VIN VIN sg13_hv_pmos w=5u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1
Ven EN VIN dc 0

* --- E1 addendum 1: non-invasive divider replica (tb_dcsweep's, issue #31).
* XRrep_top/XRrep_bot are byte-identical copies of the XRtop/XRbot lines
* above; i(vdivsense) IS the real divider's standing current at this
* corner/temperature, and (v(vout)/2)/i(vdivsense) its per-leg resistance.
Erep REPTOP 0 VOUT 0 1.0
Vdivsense REPTOP REPT dc 0
XRrep_top REPT REPFB 0 rhigh w=1e-6 l=25.43e-6 m=1 b=7
XRrep_bot REPFB 0 0 rhigh w=1e-6 l=25.43e-6 m=1 b=7

* --- E1 addendum 2: the operating-point parameter save list. The inner
* device paths follow the PDK subckt wrappers (see header). The nodes and
* source currents are saved explicitly because the fleet's klt 0.5.0
* runner emits NO `save all` of its own -- with only a device-parameter
* .save card, the node vectors would not exist and the runner's liveness
* `.meas` (and the rawfile rebuild of every v()/i() column) would fail.
* Order matters: it must match wrdata_rows' e1op token contract in
* batch_backend.py and e1_oppoints.py's QUANTITIES (all three fail closed
* on a mismatch).
.save v(vout) v(eaout) v(fb) v(fbamp) v(vref) v(en) v(ibias) v(xamp.g1) v(xamp.mz) v(xamp.n1) v(xamp.tail) v(xamp.enb) v(reptop) i(vdivsense) i(vin) i(vbreak) @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xmen.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xmen.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xmen.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xmbdis.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xmbdis.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xmbdis.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmb0.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmb0.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmb0.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmtail.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmtail.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmtail.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmload2.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmload2.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmload2.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xminp.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xamp.xminp.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xamp.xminp.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xminn.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xamp.xminn.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xamp.xminn.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xminvp.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xamp.xminvp.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xamp.xminvp.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmn1.nsg13_hv_nmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmn1.nsg13_hv_nmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmn1.nsg13_hv_nmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmn2.nsg13_hv_nmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmn2.nsg13_hv_nmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmn2.nsg13_hv_nmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmn3.nsg13_hv_nmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmn3.nsg13_hv_nmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmn3.nsg13_hv_nmos[gds] @n.xamp.xminvn.nsg13_hv_nmos[ids] @n.xamp.xminvn.nsg13_hv_nmos[gm] @n.xamp.xminvn.nsg13_hv_nmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmpd.nsg13_hv_nmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmpd.nsg13_hv_nmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmpd.nsg13_hv_nmos[gds] @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[cgs] @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[cgd] @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[cdd] @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[vth] @n.xamp.xmn3.nsg13_hv_nmos[cgs] @n.xamp.xmn3.nsg13_hv_nmos[cgd]

.control
pre_osdi /tmp/kt155/src/pdks/ihp-open-pdk/ihp-sg13cmos5l/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi /tmp/kt155/src/pdks/ihp-open-pdk/ihp-sg13cmos5l/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi /tmp/kt155/src/pdks/ihp-open-pdk/ihp-sg13cmos5l/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/mosvar.osdi
pre_osdi /tmp/kt155/src/pdks/ihp-open-pdk/ihp-sg13cmos5l/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/r3_cmc.osdi
pre_osdi /tmp/kt155/src/pdks/ihp-open-pdk/ihp-sg13cmos5l/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/cap_cmomi.osdi
pre_osdi /tmp/kt155/src/pdks/ihp-open-pdk/ihp-sg13cmos5l/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/cap_cmomf.osdi

save all
op
echo "E1OP_VOUT_OP $&v(vout)"
dc vin 3.299 3.301 0.001
wrdata /home/ubuntu/GitHub/sg13g2-ldo/.loom/worktrees/issue-158/sim/ldo-cmos5l-pvt-sweep/corners/20261012-114732-405078c7/e1op_dyn_ss_125c_rbcs_i0ua_c1000nf_e0mohm_dc.csv v(vout) v(eaout) v(fb) v(fbamp) v(vref) v(en) v(ibias) v(xamp.g1) v(xamp.mz) v(xamp.n1) v(xamp.tail) v(xamp.enb) v(reptop) i(vdivsense) i(vin) i(vbreak) @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xmen.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xmen.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xmen.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xmbdis.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xmbdis.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xmbdis.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmb0.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmb0.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmb0.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmtail.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmtail.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmtail.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmload2.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmload2.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmload2.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xminp.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xamp.xminp.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xamp.xminp.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xminn.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xamp.xminn.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xamp.xminn.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xminvp.nsg13_hv_pmos[ids] @n.xamp.xminvp.nsg13_hv_pmos[gm] @n.xamp.xminvp.nsg13_hv_pmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmn1.nsg13_hv_nmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmn1.nsg13_hv_nmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmn1.nsg13_hv_nmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmn2.nsg13_hv_nmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmn2.nsg13_hv_nmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmn2.nsg13_hv_nmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmn3.nsg13_hv_nmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmn3.nsg13_hv_nmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmn3.nsg13_hv_nmos[gds] @n.xamp.xminvn.nsg13_hv_nmos[ids] @n.xamp.xminvn.nsg13_hv_nmos[gm] @n.xamp.xminvn.nsg13_hv_nmos[gds] @n.xamp.xmpd.nsg13_hv_nmos[ids] @n.xamp.xmpd.nsg13_hv_nmos[gm] @n.xamp.xmpd.nsg13_hv_nmos[gds] @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[cgs] @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[cgd] @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[cdd] @n.xmpass.nsg13_hv_pmos[vth] @n.xamp.xmn3.nsg13_hv_nmos[cgs] @n.xamp.xmn3.nsg13_hv_nmos[cgd]
